title: Blue
key: G major
time: 4/4

# Beyonce / Boots, from the published piano-vocal arrangement, bars 1-20.
# Hybrid arrangement. The left hand is as written; the right hand is thinned to
# the notes sounding at each left-hand strike, so both hands always land
# together. The sung melody in between is dropped - it runs in sixteenths
# against a half-note bass and is not a note-reading exercise.
#
# G major, so a written F is F#. The two colours the intro alternates are
# G6 = [B3 D4 E4 G4] and Gmaj7(add13) = [B3 D4 E4 F4].

# Bars 1-4, piano intro. Both hands already strike together as written.
RH: [B3 D4 E4 G4]h [B3 D4 E4 G4]q [B3 D4 E4 G4]q
LH: [G2 D3 G3]h    [G2 D3 G3]q    [G2 D3 G3]q

RH: [B3 D4 E4 F4]h [B3 D4 E4 F4]q [B3 D4 E4 F4]q
LH: [G2 D3 G3]h    [G2 D3 G3]q    [G2 D3 G3]q

RH: [B3 D4 E4 G4]h [B3 D4 E4 G4]q [B3 D4 E4 G4]q
LH: [G2 D3 G3]h    [G2 D3 G3]q    [G2 D3 G3]q

# Bar 4 ends on the melody's pickup, and the bass turns to the major seventh.
RH: [B3 D4 E4 F4]h [B3 D4 E4 F4]q D4q
LH: [G2 D3 G3]h    [G2 D3 G3]q    [G2 D3 F3]q

# Bars 5-8, verse. From here the right hand is the thinned melody line - but a
# note the score ties or dots is held, not re-struck, so from here the left
# hand strikes alone underneath it. Bar 5's semiquaver A3-G3 pickup is not
# transcribed, and nor is any tie across a barline: the format has neither.
RH: B3w
LH: [G2 D3 G3]h [G2 D3 G3]q [G2 D3 G3]q

RH: B3h.                      D4q
LH: [G2 D3 F3]h  [G2 D3 F3]q  [G2 D3 F3]q

RH: [B3 D4]h    [B3 D4 F4]q  E4q
LH: [G2 D3 G3]h [G2 D3 G3]q  [G2 D3 G3]q

RH: [B3 D4]h    [D4 F4 D5]q [D4 F4 B4]q
LH: [G2 D3 F3]h [G2 D3 F3]q [G2 D3 F3]q

# Bars 9-12. Am7, then D - the left hand moves to half-note dyads.
RH: [C4 G4 B4]w
LH: [E3 A3]h    [E3 A3]h

RH: [C4 G4 B4]h [E4 G4 D5]h
LH: [E3 A3]h    [E3 A3]h

RH: [D4 F4 B4]h [D4 F4 A4]h
LH: [D3 A3]h    [D3 A3]h

# The right hand is tied in from bar 11 and rests on beat 3, so it holds until
# the D4 that leads back into the verse.
RH: [D4 F4 A4]h.            D4q
LH: [D3 A3]h    [D3 A3]h

# Bars 13-16 repeat the verse.
RH: B3w
LH: [G2 D3 G3]h [G2 D3 G3]q [G2 D3 G3]q

RH: B3h.                      D4q
LH: [G2 D3 F3]h  [G2 D3 F3]q  [G2 D3 F3]q

RH: [B3 D4]h    [B3 D4 F4]q  E4q
LH: [G2 D3 G3]h [G2 D3 G3]q  [G2 D3 G3]q

RH: B3h         [D4 F4 D5]q [D4 F4 B4]q
LH: [G2 D3 F3]h [G2 D3 F3]q [G2 D3 F3]q

# Bars 17-20, written as a repeat of 9-12 but for bar 17: where bar 9 ties its
# chord across beat 3, bar 17 strikes it again. Bar 20 holds its chord.
RH: [C4 G4 B4]h [C4 G4 B4]h
LH: [E3 A3]h    [E3 A3]h

RH: [C4 G4 B4]h [E4 G4 D5]h
LH: [E3 A3]h    [E3 A3]h

RH: [D4 F4 B4]h [D4 F4 A4]h
LH: [D3 A3]h    [D3 A3]h

RH: [D4 F4 A4]w
LH: [D3 A3]h    [D3 A3]h
